            desc:
              '''
              This OTP partition is used to capture the state of each key in ROT_OWNER_AUTH_SLOT0.
              Each key can be in one of the following states: BLANK, ENABLED, DISABLED. The
              encoded values are such that transitions between BLANK -> ENABLED ->  DISABLED are
              Possible without causing ECC errors (this is a mechanism similar to how we manage
              life cycle state transitions). The partition is left unlocked to allow STATE
              updates in the field. The ROM_EXT is required to lock access to the OTP Direct
              Access Interface to prevent DoS attacks from malicious code executing on Silicon
              Owner partitions. DAI write locking is available.
              '''
